# 3b Robinhood Agentic — scheduled jobs.
# Install with:  crontab -e   (paste, then verify with:  crontab -l)
#
# PATHS ARE DELIBERATELY NOT ABSOLUTE-PERSONAL. `$HOME` is expanded because cron runs each command
# through /bin/sh; adjust the sub-path if your checkout lives elsewhere. The repo directory name
# contains a SPACE, so the path is quoted and the job is invoked through bash — cron splits an
# unquoted command on whitespace and would otherwise treat "Robinhood" as an argument.

CRON_TZ=America/New_York

# ── Daily marking: the equity curve ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Syncs the broker mirror, loads the day's closes, then marks the book. 17:15 ET is after the
# 16:00 close with room for the vendor to publish the daily bar. Weekdays only; the job skips
# market holidays itself via market_calendar.
#
# This one is NOT optional if the performance page is meant to mean anything. A missed day is a
# permanent hole: a live mark is refused once it is more than 3 days old and must then be
# backfilled as an explicitly historical mark.
15 17 * * 1-5 /usr/bin/env bash "$HOME/projects/3b. Robinhood Agentic/bin/nightly_marks.sh"

# ── Fallback account snapshot, every minute ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The backend reads Alpaca live on every request, so this does NOT make the dashboard fresher. It
# keeps the FALLBACK file current — what gets served if the broker stops answering. Before this
# existed the fallback was a July Robinhood export of a book that no longer exists, refreshable
# only by a button whose host daemon shelled out to wt.exe.
# Failures do NOT go to cron mail — this machine has no MTA, so cron output is discarded. They go
# through bin/lib_notify.sh: a log under ~/.local/state/agentic plus a desktop notification.
* * * * * /usr/bin/env bash "$HOME/projects/3b. Robinhood Agentic/bin/alpaca_sync.sh"

# ── Stack health, every 5 minutes ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# On 2026-08-18 the rh-db container stopped existing — killed, not stopped — and every
# database-backed page served 503 for five minutes with nothing watching. This checks the
# containers, that Postgres actually answers, that the dashboard responds through Caddy, that the
# minute job is still writing, and that these cron entries are installed at all.
#
# Add --repair to have it recreate rh-db when the container is MISSING (idempotent; the volume is
# external so data is never touched). It still alerts and still exits non-zero when it does, because
# a stack that quietly heals a recurring fault teaches you it never happened. Left off until the
# failure has been seen at least once.
*/5 * * * * /usr/bin/env bash "$HOME/projects/3b. Robinhood Agentic/bin/stack_health.sh" --quiet

# ── Database backup, nightly ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 22:30 ET, after the 17:15 marking run has finished writing.
#
# bin/db_backup.sh existed, worked, and had NEVER been scheduled: the newest dump was three weeks
# old, predating the Alpaca migration, the seeded book, every debate record, the fundamentals
# history and two schema migrations. Restoring it would have produced a database from a different
# era of the project.
#
# That gap mattered more once the engine-generated debate records left git (see .gitignore): the
# database became the only durable copy of a corpus that costs real tokens to produce — ~390 model
# calls a day — and rh-db has already vanished once, on 2026-08-18.
30 22 * * * /usr/bin/env bash "$HOME/projects/3b. Robinhood Agentic/bin/db_backup.sh"

# ── Twice-daily cycle ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Refresh the fallback snapshot, then run the cycle in the backend container: scan the universe,
# debate every held position, write logs/reports/<date>-<phase>.md.
#
# Twice a day is the point — news breaks intraday, so a position worth holding at the open is not
# automatically worth holding at the close.
#
# COST. Each debate fans out a jury: measured at ~12 API calls and ~19k tokens per position. At
# fifteen positions that is ~180 calls per cycle, twice a day. The `cycle_max_debates` parameter
# (Parameters page) caps how many positions get debated without a redeploy — 0 means all of them —
# and every debate record now carries its own token usage, so the spend is auditable rather than
# estimated.
#
# Failures go to bin/lib_notify.sh (log + desktop notification), not to cron mail, which this
# machine discards.

# Market OPEN 09:30 ET → run at 09:32 (let the open print settle). Mon–Fri.
32 9 * * 1-5 /usr/bin/env bash "$HOME/projects/3b. Robinhood Agentic/bin/scheduled_cycle.sh" open

# Market CLOSE 16:00 ET → run at 16:02. Mon–Fri.
2 16 * * 1-5 /usr/bin/env bash "$HOME/projects/3b. Robinhood Agentic/bin/scheduled_cycle.sh" close

# ── Market Mover brief sync, every 30 minutes ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Pulls the published brief and atomically rewrites data/market_mover/latest.json, which
# backend/app/routers/market_context.py reads. The route makes no outbound call of its own
# (ADR-001), so this job is the only thing that keeps the Market page current.
#
# OWNERSHIP, since Joe's note left it open: the backend runs on THIS machine, in the `deploy`
# compose project, administered by Jared. So the cron is ours, not an ops task elsewhere.
#
# Safe to run often and safe to run early. A non-200, non-JSON, or non-object response exits 1 and
# leaves the existing file untouched, so a transient upstream hiccup never blanks the Market page —
# and until Market Mover first publishes, every run is a clean no-op.
#
# Stdlib only, so it runs on the host python3 with no venv. DATA_DIR must match the path the
# backend container has mounted (../data:/app/data), which is the repo's own data/ directory.
*/30 * * * * cd "$HOME/projects/3b. Robinhood Agentic" && /usr/bin/env DATA_DIR="$HOME/projects/3b. Robinhood Agentic/data" python3 backend/scripts/sync_market_mover_brief.py >> "$HOME/.local/state/agentic/mm-brief-sync.log" 2>&1

# ── Intraday ratio log, every 30 minutes during the session ───────────────────────────────────
# Issue #133. One observation per security in scope (held / debated / proposed): price, market cap,
# volume, and the price-derived ratios, each carrying a lineage FK to the statement row its
# denominators came from and the formula version that computed them.
#
# The RANGE is deliberately wider than regular trading hours (13:00-21:00 UTC covers 09:00-17:00 ET
# year-round, so it survives the DST shift without editing). The job gates itself on
# market_calendar's session_open/session_close, so a run outside the session records a 'skipped'
# row with the reason and writes no observation — a price that has not moved since Friday is not an
# observation, it is the same one again. Half-days close correctly for the same reason.
0,30 13-21 * * 1-5 /usr/bin/env bash "$HOME/projects/3b. Robinhood Agentic/bin/db_collect_intraday.sh" >> "$HOME/.local/state/agentic/intraday.log" 2>&1
